---
description: Use StatsHawk MCP tools for real sports statistics instead of estimating from training data.
alwaysApply: false
---

When the user asks for scores, standings, box scores, rosters, game logs,
injuries, player props, hit rates, matchups, or betting lines, use the
StatsHawk MCP tools. Do not invent numbers from memory. Arithmetic on
tool-returned values is allowed.

- Resolve players with `search_player` before any person-keyed call.
- Resolve games with `search_games` (or `get_mlb_matchups` for MLB slates)
  before box scores, play-by-play, or odds. Those tools are team-match
  only — not golf, tennis, F1, or MMA events.
- Use `get_player_props` for averages and hit rates on every plan.
- Every raw number must come from a tool result. If a stat is missing,
  say so.
- Do not call StatsHawk live or real-time. It is ingested data. Cite a
  through-date only when the payload includes a verified coverage date
  (kickoff or game date), never an edition span or retrieval time.
- For prop hit rates, report `hit_rates.<window>.games`, not the card's
  top-level `games`. Odds are pregame, not in-play.
- On 401, ask the user to reconnect StatsHawk in Customize. Retry
  transient 5xx at most twice. On `QUOTA_EXCEEDED`, stop — do not walk
  box scores. They consume the same exhausted allowance.
